\newlabel{fig:ladder}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Behavior lags the decomposition that the state supports.} Each point scores one system on parts new to the probe, by a linear probe of its state (horizontal) and by its own output (vertical), each scaled from a blend, chance or word order (0) to exact recovery (1). Bars span models, architectures or relations. Glyph networks, recursive composers, image encoders and diffusion models sit below the diagonal, and a new decoder on a frozen glyph state lifts behavior (green). Image and diffusion points use fixed quadrants, and open circles move the photographs. Language models that answer by meaning sit near the diagonal, and OLMo-2 7B answers beyond our linear probes.\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
