\newlabel{fig:intro}{{5}{15}{\textbf {Some wholes give their parts back, and others blend them.} Each column composes two parts into a whole. Placing an avocado on an armchair, setting two photographs side by side and naming two nouns in a sentence keep each part in its role, so the whole comes apart again (blue). An avocado-shaped armchair and the pixel average of two photographs merge the parts, and many pairs of parts give the same whole (red). Canva's text-to-image tool generated the avocado and armchair images \citep [after][]{openai2021dalle}, and the photographs come from Tiny-ImageNet \citep {le2015tiny}.\relax }{figure.caption.9}{}}
